Actual-source cap-backed refill must enter int(F), genuinely move the
retained contact core, or use new diameter constraints. Core local isolation
blocks an automatic restoration near the old deleted labels. The restricted
spoke comparison does not force a discrete injection in the canonical dense
core, and no uniform cap cloud chart has been proved.

The exact outstanding lemma is Section 7 of the finite-release report:
an actual nonlocal equal-cardinality refill after the unloaded stress cut,
using the paired caps and all full-source lower/upper distances. Exterior
caps remain open. No other worker's owner/train problem is attacked.

