### Continued packet-count attack: exact low-angle barrier

Composed the tip displacement gap with full-source contact minimality.
The completely guarded open cap cell has capacity exactly |S_Q|:
old isolates can be perturbed inward preserving their strict margins;
one additional packet point would pay any deleted contact vertex and
contradict canonical minimality. At a tip angle <=60 degrees the missing
guard is redundant, so deleting that actual diameter endpoint adds zero
strict capacity. The same holds for an internal wall vertex of angle
<=120 degrees with both unit neighbors guarded. If every bank guard has
its applicable angle bound, even the joint relaxed regions have exactly
their old populations and cannot cross the +4 threshold.

This is a proved finite failure of the fixed-wall strict refill mechanism
for those source geometries. It does not show the geometries occur in
canonical sources and does not close the cap branch. A packet in this
regime has to use a genuinely coupled exact-contact construction or move
the retained core/walls, or a whole-source strict diameter competitor.
The precise arbitrary-cell source population remains the unproved link;
Worker 1's closed-wall integer rounding still does not supply it.

